B.akS=new A.hB("1. Introduction",'ClassRealm ("we," "our," or "the System") is committed to protecting the privacy, confidentiality, and security of personal and academic information of all students, parents/guardians, teachers, and administrators at Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School (EBSIS). This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we process, analyze, and store it, and how users may exercise their rights\u2014including account and data deletion\u2014in strict compliance with Republic Act No. 10173, otherwise known as the Data Privacy Act of 2012, and its Implementing Rules and Regulations.')
B.al5=new A.hB("2. Information We Collect","We collect only the minimum personal, academic, and security data necessary to deliver official school management and learning services:\n\n\u2022 Students: Full Name, Learner Reference Number (LRN), Verified Personal or School Email Address, Date of Birth, Gender, Grade Level, and Section.\n\u2022 Parents/Guardians: Full Name, Verified Email Address, Contact/Mobile Number, Relationship to the linked student(s), and linked Student LRN(s).\n\u2022 Teachers & Administrators: Full Name, Email Address, Contact Number, Subject Specialization, Consultation Hours, and optional public faculty directory information.\n\u2022 RFID and Attendance Data: Assigned School RFID Card Identifier, daily time-in/time-out scan timestamps, attendance status (Present, Late, Absent, Excused), and campus/classroom attendance scanner records.\n\u2022 Academic, Classwork, and Performance Analytics Data: Written Works (WW), Performance Tasks (PT), Quarterly Examination (EX) scores, uploaded activity submissions and files, computed initial and transmuted grades (under DepEd Order No. 15, s. 2026), class rankings, learning trajectory indicators, and teacher feedback.\n\u2022 Assessment Integrity Telemetry: During active online quizzes and exams only, the System logs application focus changes (tab switches, window minimize or focus loss, and copy attempts) to uphold examination integrity. ClassRealm does NOT record camera video, microphone audio, personal photos, contacts, or device GPS location.\n\u2022 Account & Session Security Metadata: Device session identifiers, login timestamps, email verification records, and failed authentication counters used solely to prevent unauthorized account access and ensure single-session safety.")
B.akY=new A.hB("3. How We Use Your Information","Your data is processed strictly for legitimate educational, institutional, and campus safety purposes:\n\u2022 Authenticating user identity and providing secure role-based access to the Admin, Teacher, Student, and Parent portals;\n\u2022 Recording, computing, and reporting daily attendance (including DepEd School Form 2 exports) and quarterly academic grades;\n\u2022 Generating real-time Performance Analytics to help teachers identify learners who are advancing or who need academic support;\n\u2022 Delivering real-time attendance warnings, grade releases, and official school broadcast notifications to students and linked parents/guardians;\n\u2022 Sending One-Time Passwords (OTPs), account verification codes, and security alerts via email;\n\u2022 Maintaining examination integrity during digital assessments and protecting portal security.\n\nWe do NOT sell, rent, trade, or use student, parent, or teacher personal data for commercial advertising or third-party marketing.")
B.akM=new A.hB("4. Secure Local Device Storage and Cloud Synchronization","When using the mobile application in areas with weak or intermittent internet connectivity, ClassRealm temporarily stores essential academic and attendance records in secure local storage on your device. Once an internet connection is restored, these records are transmitted over encrypted HTTPS/TLS connections to our secure school cloud system. Logging out of your account immediately clears active session tokens from your device.")
B.akP=new A.hB("5. Authorized Infrastructure & Data Processing Partners","To ensure reliable, high-availability service for the school community, ClassRealm utilizes trusted enterprise cloud infrastructure for encrypted authentication, database hosting, file storage, and email verification delivery. These services process data strictly on behalf of Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School under strict confidentiality and security agreements. Student personal identities (names, LRNs, emails, and grades) are never shared with external marketing entities or unauthorized third parties.")
B.al0=new A.hB("6. Data Sharing, Visibility, and 18+ Student Privacy Rights",'\u2022 Strict Access Control: Access to student data is strictly restricted to the student themselves, their assigned subject teachers, class adviser, authorized school administrators, and verified linked parents/guardians.\n\u2022 Adult Student Privacy Rights (18+): Under Republic Act No. 10173, students who have reached eighteen (18) years of age and above may independently enable or restrict parent/guardian visibility of their Quarterly Term Grades and Final Grades through the "Parent / Guardian Privacy Controls" in Student Settings. Daily campus attendance and emergency safety notifications remain visible to linked parents/guardians for campus safety.')
B.akN=new A.hB("7. Data Security Measures","We implement organizational, physical, and technical safeguards to protect your records against unauthorized access, alteration, or loss. These include encrypted HTTPS/TLS data transmission, secure salted password hashing, strict role-based access restrictions, One-Time Password (OTP) verification for sensitive changes, single-session login protection, and automated rate-limiting against unauthorized login attempts.")
B.akX=new A.hB("8. Data Retention Policy","Personal and academic records are retained only for the duration of the active Academic School Year and for the mandatory retention period required by Department of Education (DepEd) school record-keeping regulations. Inactive or graduated accounts are archived and purged in accordance with official school administration schedules.")
B.akV=new A.hB("9. Account and Data Deletion Policy (Google Play & RA 10173 Compliance)",'Users (Students, Parents/Guardians, and Teachers) have the right to request the deletion of their ClassRealm user account and associated personal portal data at any time:\n\n\u2022 In-School Request: Submit a request directly to your Class Adviser (for Students and Parents) or to the School System Administrator / ICT Coordinator at Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School.\n\u2022 Email Request: Send an email with the subject line "ClassRealm Account Deletion Request" to the ClassRealm System Administrator / Support Team using your registered email address, stating your Full Name, User Role (Student, Parent, or Teacher), and registered Email or LRN.\n\u2022 Verification & Timeline: To protect against unauthorized deletion, the Administrator or Adviser will verify the requester\'s identity and process the account deletion within seven (7) to fourteen (14) school days.\n\u2022 Deleted vs. Retained Records: Upon approval, your login credentials, portal profile, device session tokens, and personal app access are permanently deleted. Official academic grades and attendance records required by the Department of Education (DepEd) as part of official school registries remain under the custody of Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School until the end of the mandatory DepEd retention period.')
B.al_=new A.hB("10. Your Rights Under the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173)","As a data subject under Philippine law, you are entitled to the following rights:\n\u2022 Right to be Informed: To know how your personal data is collected and used.\n\u2022 Right to Access: To request reasonable access to your personal and academic records stored in the System.\n\u2022 Right to Rectification: To dispute and request correction of any inaccurate, outdated, or incomplete personal information.\n\u2022 Right to Object & Erasure/Blocking: To object to unauthorized processing or request deletion of personal data, subject to mandatory DepEd record-keeping laws.\n\u2022 Right to Data Portability: To request a structured copy of your academic records in accordance with school guidelines.")
B.al2=new A.hB("11. Contact Information","For privacy inquiries, data correction requests, or account deletion requests, please coordinate with:\n\u2022 Data Protection / Support Team: ClassRealm Development Team\n\u2022 Institution: Eduardo Barretto Senior Integrated School (Calamba City, Laguna)\n\u2022 Contact Channel: Your Class Adviser, or the official ClassRealm Development Team.")
